        "## 4.3 Sensitivity helpers\n",
        "\n",
        "Section 6.5 checks how robust the main probabilities are. To make this easy, we publish three alternative frames, all built from `df` so they carry the same event columns:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `df_trim`: `df` without the worst 1% of reward values (reward below the 1st percentile, about -0.609).\n",
        "- `df_no_fb`: `df` without Fairbanks (the coldest city, which may drive the COLD and HOT events).\n",
        "- `df_pid`: only the baseline policy `pid_water`, with the noisy controller removed.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Event definitions and thresholds stay fixed in all three frames.** For example HE uses the 75th percentile from the full data, and BAD_RUN uses the median of all 60 runs. When rows are removed, the sample space S shrinks, and each probability is recomputed as count ÷ rows of that frame."
      ]
    },
