        "- *Addition rule for three events (inclusion-exclusion):* P(A or B or C) = P(A) + P(B) + P(C) - P(A and B) - P(A and C) - P(B and C) + P(A and B and C). Adding the three probabilities counts steps in two events twice and steps in all three three times; the pair terms remove the double counts, but they also remove the triple overlap one time too many, so it is added back once.\n",
