        "**Interpretation.** The *level* of each probability moves with the preprocessing and with the threshold: P(HP) falls from 0.2007 to about 0.193 (trim), 0.183 (no Fairbanks) and 0.174 (clean policy only), and P(HP | OCC) from 0.503 to about 0.49, 0.48 and 0.43. A stricter threshold (-0.2) shrinks P(HP) to about 0.08 and a looser one (-0.05) raises it to about 0.34, so every number is conditional on our threshold choice. Dropping one building at a time moves P(HP | OCC) within a narrow range, so no single building drives the result. The *ordering* of the findings is robust: occupied >> empty, Fairbanks and Phoenix > Atlanta, noisy > clean (cells marked NaN are not testable because the removed group is part of the comparison). Conclusion: our qualitative findings are stable; the exact levels are specific to this threshold, these 60 runs and these two baseline policies.\n",
